From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:55:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ipq40xx: give the watchdog its sysfs attributes

qualcommax builds CONFIG_WATCHDOG_SYSFS and ipq40xx does not, so on an
ipq40xx unit (the Arista W-118) /sys/class/watchdog/watchdog0 has no
state, timeout, timeleft or bootstatus, while every qualcommax unit has
them. The watchdog itself runs either way. Enable the attributes, so a
unit's watchdog state and the reason for its last reset read the same
way on every model.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/target/linux/ipq40xx/config-6.18 b/target/linux/ipq40xx/config-6.18
--- a/target/linux/ipq40xx/config-6.18
+++ b/target/linux/ipq40xx/config-6.18
@@ -525,6 +525,7 @@ CONFIG_USE_OF=y
 CONFIG_VFP=y
 CONFIG_VFPv3=y
 CONFIG_WATCHDOG_CORE=y
+CONFIG_WATCHDOG_SYSFS=y
 CONFIG_XPS=y
 CONFIG_XXHASH=y
 CONFIG_XZ_DEC_ARM=y
